after a dangerous journey these refugees  from de batsilva have finally reached a  safe haven  they're at a train station in the city  of kharkiv they have to fill out  paperwork  27 year old valerie arrived last friday  the ordeal has left him very shaken  my sister is still in  she has three kids she can't leave she  has cows a car furniture at home  even though the garage has already been  destroyed she won't leave she's afraid  to leave home with her kids  he's planning to go stay with friends in  the west of ukraine away from the  fighting but many here don't have that  option  i'm also from dubai  i don't know what to do  i arrived without any clothes shoes or  money what should we do please help us  we don't have a flat everything was  destroyed  the ukrainian army recently lost control  of the nearby town of vulgarsk after  heavy fighting now ukrainian officials  are struggling to complete a civilian  evacuation of the area  and to offer beds for the refugees  on the outskirts of kharkiv a polish aid  agency has set up emergency  accommodation  irena malieva was brought to the  settlement on the outskirts of town by  friends from  kharkiv were lucky we left so early in  the morning it was quiet and there was  little shooting  that's how we got out safely  she didn't wait for any official  evacuation before deciding to drive to  kharkiv when she arrived at the camp  there were barely any places left  the fighting is leaving large numbers of  people displaced many have nowhere to  turn
 

